{"prompt":"write a unit test for this function\n\n```python\ndef parse_duration(text):\n    \"\"\"Parse strings like '1h30m' or '45s' into seconds.\"\"\"\n    units = {\"d\": 86400, \"h\": 3600, \"m\": 60, \"s\": 1}\n    total, number = 0, \"\"\n    for ch in text.strip().lower():\n        if ch.isdigit():\n            number += ch\n        elif ch in units:\n            if not number:\n                raise ValueError(f\"missing number before {ch!r}\")\n            total += int(number) * units[ch]\n            number = \"\"\n        else:\n            raise ValueError(f\"unexpected character {ch!r}\")\n    if number:\n        raise ValueError(\"trailing number without a unit\")\n    return total\n```","tier":2,"route":"simple-code"}
{"prompt":"```ts\nexport async function retry<T>(fn: () => Promise<T>, attempts = 3, delayMs = 200): Promise<T> {\n  let last: unknown;\n  for (let i = 0; i < attempts; i++) {\n    try {\n      return await fn();\n    } catch (e) {\n      last = e;\n      await new Promise((r) => setTimeout(r, delayMs * 2 ** i));\n    }\n  }\n  throw last;\n}\n```\ncan you write a unit test for this? use vitest","tier":2,"route":"simple-code"}
{"prompt":"add a docstring to this method\n\npublic static string Slugify(string title)\n{\n    var builder = new StringBuilder(title.Length);\n    bool dash = false;\n    foreach (char c in title.ToLowerInvariant())\n    {\n        if (char.IsLetterOrDigit(c))\n        {\n            builder.Append(c);\n            dash = false;\n        }\n        else if (!dash && builder.Length > 0)\n        {\n            builder.Append('-');\n            dash = true;\n        }\n    }\n    return builder.ToString().TrimEnd('-');\n}","tier":2,"route":"simple-code"}
